    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στονᾰχ-έω</span></b> , 3pl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εῦντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					3.28
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστονάχησα</span>, the only tense used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.79
			</span></i>, inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοναχῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.124
				</span></i>
			, cf. 
			<i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.573
			</span></i>:—
				Ep.
			 form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στενάχω</span>,
				<i>groan, sigh</i>, Il.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. πόντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					38.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>sigh, groan over</i> or <i>for</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				133
			</span></i> (prob. f.l., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στενάχειν</span> cj.
			Elmsl., lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				3.28
			</span></i>.</div>
